Yes, the provided contexts outline limitations on liability for the Adviser and its personnel.

Specifically, the documents state that the Adviser Employees shall generally not be subject to liability for damages or losses incurred by the Trust arising from:
*   Any error of judgment;
*   Mistake of law;
*   Any act or omission in connection with services rendered or payments made under the Agreement (or any other related matter).

However, this protection is **not absolute**. Liability *does* apply if the loss results from:
*   Willful misfeasance;
*   Bad faith;
*   Gross negligence on the part of the Adviser; or
*   Reckless disregard by the Adviser of its obligations and duties.

These limitations are stated multiple times in the context, including:

*   PFSFUNDS\_06\_26\_2020-EX-99.H OTH MAT CONT-SERVICES AGREEMENT.PDF, Page: 2 (Chunk 1)
*   PFSFUNDS\_06\_26\_2020-EX-99.H OTH MAT CONT-SERVICES AGREEMENT.PDF, Page: 2 (Chunk 2 and Chunk 3)
